# `core.autocrlf` is true on the machine these kits are rendered on, and git
# decides text-or-binary by sniffing the first few KB. A WAV whose header and
# leading samples happen to carry no NUL byte can be sniffed as text, and then
# every 0x0A in the audio becomes 0x0D 0x0A on checkout: the file grows, the
# chunk length in the header stops matching the data, and the kit either fails
# to load or plays as noise. Say it outright instead of trusting the sniff.
*.wav binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary

# Same reasoning for the images and fonts the app ships.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
